#====================================================================
# E225 - open_memstream symbol presence without a usable close contract
#====================================================================

id:                     E302
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|libc
phase:                  configuration|testing
error_signature:        PosixMemstreamTest\.CanCheckBufferWithContents|HAVE_OPEN_MEMSTREAM=1|Actual: ''

severity:               3
category:               libc-runtime-capability-detection
match_keywords:         open_memstream, fclose, fflush, cookie stream, HAVE_OPEN_MEMSTREAM, empty captured output
title:                  Gate open_memstream on its close and flush contract, not symbol presence

root_cause:             A target libc can export open_memstream while fclose rejects its cookie stream before flushing buffered data, so symbol-only CMake detection enables a capability whose observable contract is broken.
affected_scope:         CMake projects and test frameworks that use open_memstream to capture FILE output, especially cross builds that cannot run configure-time probes.
verification_cmd:       On the target, write a sub-BUFSIZ string to open_memstream, require fclose to return zero, and compare the resulting buffer; then rerun every test target that consumes the wrapper.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           behavior-probe-or-evidence-bound-disable
rec_description:        Prefer a target behavior probe that verifies write, fclose, and buffer publication. When cross configuration cannot run it, use an evidence-bound target override to disable the capability and retain the upstream fallback path.
rec_command:            Set HAVE_OPEN_MEMSTREAM=OFF only for a target whose runtime probe or libc implementation proves the close and flush contract is unusable.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               cmake-capability-probe-or-conan-toolchain-override

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      writable-real-file-capture
fallback_description:   If output comparison remains required, use a writable real file stream under TMPDIR and preserve the same readback assertions.
fallback_command:       Route capture through a normal file opened below TMPDIR and validate cleanup plus exact content.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          test-infrastructure

forbid_1_pattern:       fflush\(.*\).*fclose\(|change expected output to empty|skip the complete test target
forbid_1_reason:        A pre-flush workaround can leave the broken cookie stream unclosed, while changing references or skipping targets hides the failed runtime contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   Resource leaks or false-positive test results remain even though the immediate empty-output assertion disappears.

principles:             

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E302.md
last_updated:           2026-07-30
source_event:           gromacs/2026.3 OHOS TestUtilsUnitTests and UtilityUnitTests empty capture failures
authors:                2301_80739235
